So here's the real answer: when the count hits zero, you free. The safe pattern is to decrement and test in one step, and never touch the object after it may have been freed.

```c
if (atomic_fetch_sub_explicit(&obj->refcount, 1, memory_order_acq_rel) == 1) {
    atomic_thread_fence(memory_order_acquire);
    object_destroy(obj);
}
```

The trap interviewers look for: checking `refcount == 0` *after* the decrement rather than using the old value, which races with another thread that just incremented. Use the pre-decrement value. Also free only after all reads, and make destruction release child references first to avoid a cascade on the wrong thread.

